  "summary": "Source-fidelity audit of prose claims against Tables 1-9, Figures 1-4 and Appendix A.3. Core numbers reconcile: Tables 3/4 agreement of 33/34, Table 6 date precision of 19+10+9+5=43, Table 8 shares of 700,579 listings, and Figure 2/3/4 values against the prose. I found seven source-fidelity problems. (1) Footnote 3 says both human coders coded the Stord article not relevant, but Section 4.1 and Table 3 make it the one article on which they disagree. (2) The '2 of 34 articles (about 6 percent)' and '2 of 70 search hits' claims use distinct openings as a numerator over article and hit denominators. (3) Figure 1 says two openings took place, while Table 2 note c reports a third opening (Grettefoss) and the Status column still reads 'Planned'. (4) The Appendix A.3.2 first-type-wins rule contradicts its own bysykkelstativ example and Table 9 and Figure 2 placement of syklende. (5) Figure 2 codes sykkelmulighet as Leisure although it contains none of the Leisure word parts in Table 9. (6) The prose says the first quarter of 2024 is missing, but the stated gap is January-April 2024. (7) The 44-project count of Section 6 cannot be mapped to the pilot versus rounds 2-4 sets. Structured table markdown was not used as primary evidence because the parser-quality guidance flagged it; page text and figure images were used instead.",
